title: The Workers' Government
subtitle: Legien asks what the communists will do.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1920 and month = 4 and crisis = 0 and kapp_outcome = 3 and ending_id = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 2

= The Workers' Government

Carl Legien sits in the Chancellery, with SPD and USPD ministers and the union leaders behind him. Noske is gone. The cabinet promises to purge the army, disarm the Freikorps and put the coal mines under public control. The Centre and the Democrats call it a dictatorship of the unions.

It has no majority in the National Assembly, and elections are due in June. Legien sends word through the USPD that he would like to know where the communists stand.

- @loyal: A loyal opposition, as we promised.
- @enter: Enter the government.
- @oppose: Oppose it as a cover for the employers.

@loyal
subtitle: We vote for every purge of the army and against every concession to the employers.
on-arrival: {!
Q.wg_stance = 1;
Q.uspd_relation += 5;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
RG.ecci('lenin', 5);
!}

The cabinet does not love us. It knows where we stand.

@enter
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Communists in the ministries. Moscow will be furious, and so will our Left.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids sitting in a government with social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.wg_stance = 2;
Q.kpd_in_government = 1;
Q.government_name = 'Workers\' government (SPD, USPD, KPD, unions)';
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 15;
Q.lean_unionist += 3;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -10);
RG.news('Communists enter the workers\' government', 3);
RG.ledger('Communist ministers sat in a German government in 1920.', 'e20_ministers');
!}

A communist becomes under-secretary for the mines, and another sits on the commission for the purge of the army. Zinoviev's telegram from Moscow is short.

@oppose
subtitle: Many workers who struck in March will think we have forgotten who Kapp was.
on-arrival: {!
Q.wg_stance = 3;
Q.worker_support -= 3;
Q.uspd_relation -= 8;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

*Die Rote Fahne* calls Legien's cabinet the last line of defence of German capital.
